content.text:
I've added an **ABDM** tab to the patient page, next to Clinical History. It only appears for users who can view clinical data, the same rule the API endpoint enforces. The frontend type-check passes. I haven't opened the tab in a browser yet, so it's untested against live data.

The tab has three sections:

- **ABHA:** the patient's ABHA number and address. If the patient has none, it says so.
- **Visits shared through ABDM:** a summary line with the number of visits and how many can't yet be found from the patient's ABHA. Each visit row shows:
  - the visit name, which links to that encounter, with the facility and HIP ID underneath;
  - the record types for the visit, with types not yet announced to ABDM highlighted;
  - the link status, plus ABDM's error code and message if it refused the link;
  - the time of the last update.
- **Consents:** each consent request shows:
  - who asked, why, and the consent's status;
  - the record types and date range it covers, and when the requester must erase the data;
  - which visits it covers;
  - each time records were sent under it, with a per-visit delivery status.

If ABDM is turned off on this instance, the tab shows a message saying so instead.

The code is in [Abdm.tsx](care_fe/src/components/Patient/PatientDetailsTab/Abdm.tsx), and the tab is registered in [index.tsx](care_fe/src/components/Patient/PatientDetailsTab/index.tsx). It reads from the new `/api/v1/abdm/patient/{id}/` endpoint, which has tests. The new English text strings are at the end of `en.json`.

